From 05ec3cecfacdd5f8562de8261e86e0e862f7d3d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:04:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 094/252] feat(pypto-x): release dead SSA buffers and add
 packed AVX-512 cast/transpose/embedding kernels

The T=5 Qwen3.5-0.8B AVX-512 run was stopped at op #4 for two independent
reasons, and both are fixed here.

P1 (liveness): the vector, AVX2 and AVX-512 launch loops kept every SSA value
alive until the launch returned (6.53 GB of dead intermediates at T=5).  The
new `pypto.backends.cpu.ssa_liveness` module computes last-use indexes from the
immutable operation list and releases a value straight after its last consumer.
Parameters and function returns are pinned, so no observable value, canary or
artifact contract changes.

P2 (packed parameter-scale kernels): the host reference materialized whole
tensors as Python lists (~28 B/element), which is 13.6 GiB for the embedding
table alone.  AVX-512 now runs `cast` (f32<->bf16, RNE, bit-exact with the
reference), rank-2 `transpose` and axis-0 `embedding` as packed native kernels
over caller buffers, with ctypes-allocated destinations that never build a
Python element list.  The kernel choice is a single predicate shared by the
compiler metadata and the runtime, so a declared mode cannot disagree with the
executed one; everything not covered stays `host_reference`.

The artifact payload version moves to 2, the lowering version to 3 and the
native ABI marker to `pypto-x.cpu.avx512:3`, so payload-1 artifacts (which
advertised all three operations as host_reference) fail closed.
